{"name":"Sweet Lemon","hex":"#f7bf43","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet lemon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants that produce fruit resembling lemon or lime, but less acidic than lemon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet_lemon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweet lemon","blocks":[{"text":"Sweet lemon and sweet lime refer to groups of citrus hybrids that contain low acid pulp and juice. They are hybrids often similar to non-sweet lemons or limes, but with less citron parentage. Sweet limes and lemons are not sharply separated:"},{"text":"The sweet lime, Citrus limettioides Tan., is often confused with the sweet lemon, C. limetta Tan., which, in certain areas, is referred to as \"sweet lime\". In some of the literature, it is impossible to tell which fruit is under discussion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/%28Citrus_limetta%29_Mosambi_at_a_market_in_Seethammadhara.jpg/330px-%28Citrus_limetta%29_Mosambi_at_a_market_in_Seethammadhara.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_lemon","wikidata":"Q3241046"},{"title":"Lemon","blocks":[{"text":"The lemon is a species of small evergreen tree in the Citrus genus of the flowering plant family Rutaceae. A true lemon is a hybrid of the citron and the bitter orange. Its origins are uncertain, but some evidence suggests lemons originated during the 1st millennium BC in what is now northeastern India. Some other citrus fruits are called lemon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/P1030323.JPG/330px-P1030323.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon","wikidata":"Q500"},{"title":"Lemon (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lemon or lemon-color is a vivid yellow color characteristic of the lemon fruit. Shades of \"lemon\" may vary significantly from the fruit's actual color, including fluorescent tones and creamy hues reflective of lemon pies and confections."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg/330px-Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon_(color)","wikidata":"Q2720565"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/%28Citrus_limetta%29_Mosambi_at_a_market_in_Seethammadhara.jpg/500px-%28Citrus_limetta%29_Mosambi_at_a_market_in_Seethammadhara.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/%28Citrus_limetta%29_Mosambi_at_a_market_in_Seethammadhara.jpg/1280px-%28Citrus_limetta%29_Mosambi_at_a_market_in_Seethammadhara.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/%28Citrus_limetta%29_Mosambi_at_a_market_in_Seethammadhara.jpg/500px-%28Citrus_limetta%29_Mosambi_at_a_market_in_Seethammadhara.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Limetta","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A(Citrus_limetta)_Mosambi_at_a_market_in_Seethammadhara.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Sweet_limes_of_Salem.jpg/500px-Sweet_limes_of_Salem.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Sweet_limes_of_Salem.jpg/1280px-Sweet_limes_of_Salem.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Sweet_limes_of_Salem.jpg/500px-Sweet_limes_of_Salem.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sweet limes of Salem","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASweet_limes_of_Salem.jpg"